Put msvcm90.dll, msvcp90.dll, msvcr90.dll and Microsoft.VC90.CRT.manifest
in this directory for Windows builds using a VS 2008 / VC 9.0 compiler.

For x64 (--config=x64) builds, also create an amd64/ subdirectory and put the
amd64 copies of msvcm90.dll, msvcp90.dll, msvcr90.dll and
Microsoft.VC90.CRT.manifest there (from VC\redist\amd64\Microsoft.VC90.CRT),
plus an amd64 application manifest amd64/vc90_app.manifest (a copy of
vc90_app.manifest with processorArchitecture="amd64").  The build tools
(idlc, regmerge, ...) run on the x64 host and are built x64, so they need the
amd64 CRT; the crt_dlls / vc90_app_manifest filegroups select() the amd64
variants for the x64 configuration.
